{"id":"odia_eng_prob_set_02","title":"English & Odia Mock — Probable Set 2","questions":[{"number":1,"section":"English Language","contextText":null,"imageAssetPath":null,"questionText":"May you live happily and long! Identify the meaning expressed.","options":["Desire","Approval","Happiness","Wish"],"correctIndex":3},{"number":2,"section":"English Language","contextText":null,"imageAssetPath":null,"questionText":"Which is the most polite request?","options":["Will you lend me your scooter?","Would you lend me your scooter, please?","Can you lend me your scooter, please?","Shall I take your scooter on loan?"],"correctIndex":1},{"number":3,"section":"English Language","contextText":null,"imageAssetPath":null,"questionText":"He has been sleeping for five hours. What does this imply?","options":["He is sleeping for hours.","He has lost sense of time.","He is still sleeping.","He will not wake up now."],"correctIndex":2},{"number":4,"section":"English Language","contextText":null,"imageAssetPath":null,"questionText":"Only graduates are eligible ______ this post.","options":["to","for","with","along"],"correctIndex":1},{"number":5,"section":"English Language","contextText":null,"imageAssetPath":null,"questionText":"The girls sang songs while the boys played hockey. The actions occurred ______.","options":["at some other time","at the same time","at different venues","at the same venue"],"correctIndex":1},{"number":6,"section":"English Language","contextText":null,"imageAssetPath":null,"questionText":"He will be late. That is certain. Choose the best combined sentence.","options":["That will be late for him certainly.","Certainly he will be late.","It will be certain that he late for him.","It is certain that he will be late."],"correctIndex":3},{"number":7,"section":"English Language","contextText":null,"imageAssetPath":null,"questionText":"We derive nouns from verbs. From “weave” we derive ______.","options":["weaving","woven","web","warp"],"correctIndex":0},{"number":8